# Maven Resolver 2 asks every remote repository of the build for its prefix
# file, the list of group prefixes it serves, and looks up an artifact only
# where the list allows. flyway-parent, the parent POM of every Flyway
# artifact, declares two repositories that answer an anonymous request with
# 401, so every build logged a WARNING for each of them.
#
# Not asking these two ends where the 401 did: no prefix list, so no
# filtering for them, without the request and the warning. Every other
# repository, Central included, keeps its list. Drop a line once flyway-parent
# stops declaring that repository.
-Daether.remoteRepositoryFilter.prefixes.resolvePrefixFiles.flyway-community-db-support=false
-Daether.remoteRepositoryFilter.prefixes.resolvePrefixFiles.MavenFeed=false
